<div class="body" id="fhbody-186550485">
	

	
		
		<div id="text-186550485" class="p">
			
		 	
				Toyota's EV sales have jumped 127% through September, <a href="https://electrek.co/2026/10/29/toyotas-ev-sales-doubled-but-gas-cars-getting-crushed-china/">reports <em>Electrek</em></a>:

<i>Including Lexus, Toyota sold 309,766 battery electric vehicles (BEVs) globally through the first nine months of 2026, up 127.4% from the same period last year. Except for January (+87.5%), Toyota's EV sales have more than doubled every month this year compared with 2025...<br> <br>
While its EVs are catching on, Toyota Motor's global sales fell for the third straight month in September.  Toyota sold 860,107 vehicles in September, down 2.2% from the previous year.  The company said that although overall demand remained steady, sales in China fell, leading to lower overall sales than last year. Through September, Toyota sold 7.51 million vehicles globally, down 3.4%.  In China, Toyota's sales plunged nearly 20%, marking its eighth consecutive month with lower sales.  Toyota said the overall market in China "remained weak due in part to rising gasoline prices, while the market for gasoline vehicles and hybrid vehicles was particularly affected," resulting in lower sales.  In the first nine months of 2026, Toyota sold just over 1.05 million vehicles in China, 18.9% fewer than in the same period last year...  After the US, China is Toyota's second-largest market.

